] [17592186221468 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186222334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221468 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186222335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221468 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186222336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221468 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186222337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221468 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221468 #edb/ref 1045 "Fundamental Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221468 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186222332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221468 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221468 #edb/ref 1050 960.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186221468 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "bf2387fe-ebed-5568-a260-0d681cb9fd28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222332 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186222333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222332 #edb/ref 1061 594316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222332 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3b0bd285-b383-5ebb-821f-4f74a0b37719" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222332 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186222502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222333 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186222334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222333 #edb/ref 1061 594317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222333 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "aa3c7790-3ab9-5519-bad3-4f82fc8ac113" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222333 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186221420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222334 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186222335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222334 #edb/ref 1061 594320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222334 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2fe7252e-7fc7-59bb-bc32-74c452b7cf73" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222334 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186222503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222335 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186222336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222335 #edb/ref 1061 594321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222335 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2b90cd12-9695-5b6b-b407-6eed6ae7fc84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222335 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186221421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222336 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186222337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222336 #edb/ref 1061 594325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222336 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d44c84d5-4215-5318-bba2-81eb3a34ee7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222336 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186222504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222337 #edb/ref 1061 594326 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222337 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "32e0e465-9256-5f88-b771-2edff24ecd54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222337 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186221422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222502 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the homogeneous linear system\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}' = A\\mathbf{x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix.\n\nA **fundamental matrix** for this system is an $n\\times n$ matrix $\\Phi(t)$ whose columns are $n$ linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIf $\\mathbf{x}_1(t),\\dots,\\mathbf{x}_n(t)$ are linearly independent solutions, then one fundamental matrix is\n\n$$\n\\Phi(t)=\\big[\\mathbf{x}_1(t),\\dots,\\mathbf{x}_n(t)\\big].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $\\Phi(t)$ can be written in any order.\n\nLet's see an example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222502 #edb/ref 1065 14508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222502 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a7207a24-194d-59d6-b25c-f9bb4f1b0d6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222502 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222503 #edb/ref 1064 "Again, let $\\Phi(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for the linear system\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}' = A\\mathbf{x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix. The fundamental matrices have the following important properties.\n\n1\\. *Satisfies the underlying system*. Indeed, since each column of $\\Phi(t)$ is a solution of the system, we have\n\n  $$\n  \\Phi'(t) = A\\,\\Phi(t).\n  $$\n\n2\\. *Invertibility*. The columns of $\\Phi(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t,$ so\n\n  $$\n  \\det\\Phi(t)\\neq 0\n  $$\n\n  for all $t.$ In particular, $\\Phi(t)$ is invertible for all $t.$\n\n3\\. *Representation of solutions*. Every solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ of the system can be written in the form\n\n  $$\n  \\mathbf{x}(t)=\\Phi(t)\\,\\mathbf{c},\n  $$\n\n  where $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\n4\\. *Non-uniqueness*. If $C$ is any invertible constant matrix, then\n\n  $$\n  \\Psi(t)=\\Phi(t)\\,C\n  $$\n\n  is also a fundamental matrix for the same system.\n\nWe'll now get some practice." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222503 #edb/ref 1065 14509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222503 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e2fdbc29-4542-5fdc-adbd-316c5dcb6878" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222503 #edb/ref 1067 "Properties of the Fundamental Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222504 #edb/ref 1064 "For a linear system $\\mathbf{x}' = A\\mathbf{x}$ with constant $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ the **standard fundamental matrix** is the unique fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ that satisfies the initial condition\n\n$$\n\\Phi_0(0)=I_n,\n$$\n\nwhere $I_n$ is the $n \\times n$ identity matrix.\n\nFor constant matrices $A,$ the standard fundamental matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\Phi_0(t)=e^{At}.\n$$\n\nThis matrix satisfies\n\n$$\n\\Phi_0'(t)=A\\,\\Phi_0(t)\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\Phi_0(0)=I_n.\n$$\n\n**Note:** Any other fundamental matrix $\\Phi(t)$ for the same system can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\Phi(t)=\\Phi_0(t)\\,C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an invertible constant matrix.\n\nIn the next slide, we will compute the standard fundamental matrix for a specific example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222504 #edb/ref 1065 14510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222504 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4f75576c-be32-5784-9fee-e1288445728c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186222504 #edb/ref 1067 "Fundamental Matrices and Matrix Exponentials" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308916 #edb/ref 1080 "properties of invertible matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308916 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/